{"chunk_id": "a520ab28d9ae", "text": "This section depicts the terrifying night battle between the Rakshasa prince Ghatotkacha, son of Bhima, and the Kaurava forces led by Karna. After Ghatotkacha slays the Rakshasa ally Alayudha and throws his severed head before Duryodhana, panic spreads among the Kauravas. Karna enters the fray and clashes with Ghatotkacha in a spectacular duel marked by torrents of arrows and supernatural illusions. Ghatotkacha unleashes devastating magical assaults\u2014clouds raining weapons, rocks, and thunderbolts\u2014throwing the Kaurava army into chaos. As the army nears destruction, the Kauravas beg Karna to use the divine spear granted by Indra, a weapon he had reserved to kill Arjuna. Forced by desperation, Karna hurls the irresistible dart at Ghatotkacha, a momentous decision that saves the Kauravas but sacrifices his best chance to defeat Arjuna later.\nGhatotkacha slays Alayudha and devastates the Kaurava army with illusions until Karna, pressed by panic, finally uses Indra\u2019s divine dart against him.\nThemes: rakshasa warfare, illusion and supernatural battle, Karna\u2019s divine weapon, night battle chaos, sacrifice before Arjuna", "vector": [-0.0014101576525717974, -0.002891989890486002, 0.0044571650214493275, 0.014108243398368359, 0.010134465992450714, 0.03253696858882904, -0.0257762148976326, -0.013221478089690208, -0.02816314809024334, -0.02749640680849552, 0.018215369433164597, 0.010667858645319939, 0.012441390193998814, 0.006730752531439066, 0.009927776642143726, -0.0011226254282519221, 0.03224360570311546, -0.014401610009372234, 0.02234916388988495, -0.02421603910624981, -0.0017235259292647243, -0.0033103700261563063, 0.002170242602005601, 0.03187022730708122, -0.02730971947312355, 0.019042128697037697, 0.00996778067201376, -0.024816107004880905, 0.017255261540412903, -0.014201587066054344, -0.016828548163175583, -0.011527955532073975, -0.0011451280442997813, -0.006064011249691248, -0.037204157561063766, 0.0145082883536